exports[`output of every command, text and --json > take a slice for human QA > text 1`] = `
"exit 0
You now hold slice #133 "Metrics". Its step is human QA. This step is
attended: the user takes part, and you do not decide on your own.

Work in: /repo/.agents/worktrees/123-rate-limiting-133 (branch 123-rate-limiting-133)
It does not exist yet. Create it first:
  git -C /repo fetch origin 123-rate-limiting && git -C /repo worktree add --no-track /repo/.agents/worktrees/123-rate-limiting-133 -b 123-rate-limiting-133 origin/123-rate-limiting

Invoke the skill: qa
Spec: .agents/specs/123-rate-limiting/spec.md (story #123)
Read the issue: gh issue view 133 --comments
Slice PR: 123-rate-limiting-133 into 123-rate-limiting. Diff: git diff origin/123-rate-limiting...HEAD
Start from the agent's QA comment on #133: its evidence, and what it left for a person. Read the issue: gh issue view 133 --comments
Run the app from 123-rate-limiting-133 on this machine and walk the user through what is left, plus anything in the evidence they question.
Tie each remark the user brings to a criterion; a remark on a criterion fails it. For a remark outside the criteria, the user decides:
  follow up (the default): gh issue create --title "<remark>" --body "From QA of #133: <remark>" (it goes through triage)
  pull it in: it fails this item, like a criterion
  drop it: say so in the note
Every failure needs a repro. Keep screenshots, logs and command output in a directory outside the repository and finish with --evidence <dir>: shepherd pushes the files and embeds them in the comment. Do not commit them.

When the user agrees human QA is finished, run one of:
  shepherd done 133 pass [--evidence <dir>]              (the person passes QA, moves to the merge queue)
  shepherd done 133 fail "problems" [--evidence <dir>]   (put the failures with their repros in the note)

On a long step, run shepherd take 133 again now and then: it keeps your claim fresh.
If you have to stop, run: shepherd release 133
If something is wrong and a person is needed, run: shepherd escalate 133 "reason"

Do not change labels yourself. Only shepherd changes them."
`;

