exports[`output of every command, text and --json > take again while holding > text 1`] = `
"exit 0
You already held #50; the claim is refreshed. Here is its briefing again.

You now hold story #50 "Search". Its step is slicing. This step is attended:
the user takes part, and you do not decide on your own.

Work in: /repo/.agents/worktrees/50-search (branch 50-search)
It does not exist yet. Create it first:
  git -C /repo fetch origin main && git -C /repo worktree add --no-track /repo/.agents/worktrees/50-search -b 50-search origin/main

Invoke the skill: slice
Spec to work on: .agents/specs/50-search/spec.md
Create the slices in dependency order, blockers first, one command per slice:
  shepherd add-slice 50 "title" --mode afk|hil [--blocked-by <slice>]...
  --mode afk when an agent can verify every criterion, hil when a person must also look at it.
Then give each slice its body: gh issue edit <slice> --body-file <file>
Push 50-search once the slices exist, so slice PRs can target it.

When the user agrees slicing is finished, run:
  shepherd done 50

On a long step, run shepherd take 50 again now and then: it keeps your claim fresh.
If you have to stop, run: shepherd release 50
If something is wrong and a person is needed, run: shepherd escalate 50 "reason"

Do not change labels yourself. Only shepherd changes them."
`;

