exports[`output of every command, text and --json > unknown command > json 1`] = `
"exit 2
{
  "ok": false,
  "refusal": "shepherd runs work through the SDD process. Commands on an issue take its number explicitly.\\n\\n  shepherd init                          Set up this project: skills, .agents/specs/, labels\\n  shepherd next <story>                  What can be done on the story now\\n  shepherd take <issue> [--takeover]     Claim the issue and get the briefing for its step;\\n                                     --takeover takes it from a stopped session of yours\\n  shepherd done <issue> [outcome] [\\"note\\"] [--evidence <dir>]\\n                                     Finish the step; shepherd makes the transition.\\n                                     --evidence attaches the QA files in <dir>\\n  shepherd add-slice <story> \\"title\\" --mode afk|hil [--blocked-by <issue>]...\\n  shepherd escalate <issue> \\"reason\\"     Set needs-human and release the claim\\n  shepherd release <issue>               Give up the claim without a transition\\n  shepherd status <story>                Read-only overview of the story and its slices\\n  shepherd tidy [--dry-run]              Remove what belongs to closed issues\\n  shepherd dashboard [--port <n>] [--interval <duration>] [--no-open]\\n                                     Watch your work in the browser; Ctrl-C stops it\\n\\nAdd --json for machine-readable output."
}"
`;

exports[`output of every command, text and --json > unknown command > text 1`] = `
"exit 2
shepherd runs work through the SDD process. Commands on an issue take its number explicitly.

  shepherd init                          Set up this project: skills, .agents/specs/, labels
  shepherd next <story>                  What can be done on the story now
  shepherd take <issue> [--takeover]     Claim the issue and get the briefing for its step;
                                     --takeover takes it from a stopped session of yours
  shepherd done <issue> [outcome] ["note"] [--evidence <dir>]
                                     Finish the step; shepherd makes the transition.
                                     --evidence attaches the QA files in <dir>
  shepherd add-slice <story> "title" --mode afk|hil [--blocked-by <issue>]...
  shepherd escalate <issue> "reason"     Set needs-human and release the claim
  shepherd release <issue>               Give up the claim without a transition
  shepherd status <story>                Read-only overview of the story and its slices
  shepherd tidy [--dry-run]              Remove what belongs to closed issues
  shepherd dashboard [--port <n>] [--interval <duration>] [--no-open]
                                     Watch your work in the browser; Ctrl-C stops it

Add --json for machine-readable output."
`;

